      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "both",
        "summary": "dc susceptibility of 1 from 290–2 K is consistent with two Co(II) and four Tb(III) uncoupled spins (including the mononuclear Tb counteranion); χMT decreases on cooling due to anisotropy/thermal depopulation and possible weak antiferromagnetic interactions. Magnetization does not saturate at 7 T. No slow magnetic relaxation in ac studies. UV–vis absorption in MeCN is also reported.",
